    <!--
      Normal reads as aquarium blue rather than green. The hue is #BDECF6's, which is h 217 in
      CIELAB, an aqua rather than a true blue; this is that hue taken down to the green's own
      L* 60, where it is a colour in its own right instead of a wash. The chroma stops at 34
      because that is as far as h 217 reaches at that lightness in sRGB, so this is as saturated
      as the hue gets without going darker. Lightness matching the green is what keeps the pill
      label at the same 3.1:1 against white the other statuses carry.

      @color/status_green stays as it was: the auth and template screens use it for "valid", which
      is a different claim from a sensor being in its band.
    -->
