    <!--
      The analytics period selector, which is a groove with one button raised out of it.

      Day builds that the way the rest of the light scheme does: the groove is a shade below
      @color/background so it reads as cut into the page, and the raised button is the card white
      already used for every surface that sits on top of something. Night has to invert the first
      half of that - a groove below #0F1419 is black - so there the groove is the shade just above
      the page and the raised button a further step up again. Either way the pair stays one step
      apart, which is what the recess is made of.

      The labels are @color/text_muted on the groove and @color/accent on the raised button, at
      5.7:1 and 6.9:1 in day, 8.4:1 and 5.4:1 in night.
    -->
    <color name="analytics_segment_track">#FFE3E8EF</color>
    <color name="analytics_segment_selected">#FFFFFFFF</color>

    <!--
      The same groove for the bar the two chart actions sit in, but laid over the plot rather than
      on the card, so it is let down to seven tenths and the line it covers reads through it. The
      icons on top keep their own full strength, so what is traded away is the bar's opacity rather
      than their legibility.
    -->
    <color name="analytics_action_bar_track">#B3E3E8EF</color>

